WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.980
That’s quite a background.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.610
Well, up to now the President's gambit on
Cuba has been pretty much a debacle.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.960
It's been a one-sided affair.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:16.590
He's showering concessions on the regime,
and getting really nothing in return.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.620
But I'm not totally pessimistic about his
visit because I think he can salvage this

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:29.080
Cuba initiative by going to Cuba, going to
Havana, insisting on a national platform,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.650
some sort of national broadcast, and posing
to the regime this challenge: "Let Cubans

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:36.650
vote.”

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.570
Let them decide their future.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.870
That's really the problem up to now.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.070
I think the President didn't understand that
the real problem in Cuba was not U.S. policy

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.530
but the fact that the regime is a totalitarian
regime that's bent on holding onto power.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:52.370
If he makes that challenge, it will really
be a historic moment.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.260
It will be like Reagan saying: "Tear down
this wall."

00:00:55.260 --> 00:01:04.920
And a great opportunity for the Cuban people
to see the Americans as friends and seize

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.020
this opportunity.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.409
What are your ideas about empowering the Cuban
people.

00:01:09.409 --> 00:01:12.121
Please offer your comments and give us ideas
about topics you’d like us to cover in the

00:01:12.121 --> 00:01:12.130
future.

